 ## Non-negotiable brand and composition rules
 
 - Use the approved full logo lockup only; do not redraw, distort, recolour, or add a shadow to it.
+- **9:16 logo rule:** do not place the Newton School logo on any 9:16 (1080×1920, Stories/Reels) image — not in the top-left corner or anywhere else — unless the user's prompt explicitly asks for the logo on the 9:16 version. When it is asked for, use the approved lockup per the brand rules and keep it inside the safe zone (clear of the top 250 px of platform UI).
 - Preserve required clear space and minimum size. Use the approved foreground/background signature with adequate contrast.
 - Use Mona Sans for final branded text. Do not claim exact palette values that are not printed in the source guide.
 - Apply the relevant design-skill rules for the requested format. Reframe through deliberate responsive reflow, not a destructive crop or a redesign.
+- **F-pattern reading order:** an average viewer scans a creative in an F shape — first across the top, then a shorter second line, then down the left edge. Put the hook top-left, directly under the logo, with no empty band between them; make the subhook the second, shorter line beneath it; align the supporting proof (RTBs, CTA, program pill) down the left edge or starting from the left. Place the key visual on the right so it fills the top-right instead of leaving white space. Never leave the top third empty or let a hero visual push the hook down the frame. For 16:9, the copy column sits on the left with the same order; for 9:16, the same order applies below the top safe zone.
 - Keep people, logo, copy, icons, and CTAs out of each other's safe zones. Make hierarchy readable at the final delivery size.
 - Do not invent people, learner testimonials, consent, statistics, salaries, outcomes, or claims.
 
