 # Creative Engine skills decision log
 
+## 2026-10-11 — Lay out creatives for F-pattern reading
+
+- **What changed:** Added an F-pattern composition rule to the shared creative-output standards, the suite router, and the 9x16, 1x1 and 16x9 design skills: hook top-left directly under the logo, subhook as the shorter second line, RTBs/CTA aligned down the left edge, key visual on the right, and no empty top third.
+- **Why:** Review of a 4:5 creative showed the eye landing on empty top space while the hook sat mid-frame on the right. An average viewer scans in an F shape (top line, shorter second line, then down the left), so the most important copy must sit where that scan starts.
+- **Why this method:** Every image workflow already reads the shared standards before composing, and each ratio's design skill points back to the same rule, so new, refreshed and reframed outputs share one reading order.
+
+## 2026-10-11 — No logo on 9:16 images unless the prompt asks for it
+
+- **What changed:** Added a 9:16 logo rule to the shared creative-output standards, the core brand gate, the 9x16 design skill, and the new-creatives, refresh-creatives and reframe-and-resize workflows. A 9:16 (1080×1920) image gets no Newton School logo — not top-left or anywhere — unless the user's prompt explicitly requests it; if requested, the approved lockup goes inside the safe zone below the top 250 px.
+- **Why:** The Growth team does not want the logo on Stories/Reels creatives by default.
+- **Why this method:** The rule sits in the shared standards that every image workflow reads first, and each workflow that could add or keep a logo points back to it, so new, refreshed and reframed 9:16 outputs all behave the same way.
+
 ## 2026-10-09 — Save Good-rated images in one shared local folder
 
 - **What changed:** Added a tested, dependency-free save command for the image skills. It accepts a local PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF, or AVIF only after an explicit Good-rating marker, validates the file header, and copies exact bytes into one flat `approved-images/` folder with a unique filename. The folder is retained in the package but generated images are Git-ignored.
